      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T21:00:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re kicking the battery out of CONFIG_BATTERY_REVIVE_DISCONNECT state (battery still talks over i2c, but doesn\u0027t provide VBAT), right? Our typical way of getting the battery out of this state is to apply a precharge current (see common code in charge_state_v2).\n\nCan this register only be cleared with an i2c write on the Sony battery? If we had a similar universal method of kicking the battery out of disconnect, it would be much preferred to what we implement now in common code.\n\nAlso, I think you should check for safety fault before clearing this, as we do in battery_get_disconnect_state().",
